.TH "LANGUAGEMODEL.APPEND" "3JS" "August 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LanguageModel.append \- LanguageModel: append() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]append()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R]
interface adds content to the session\(cqs context window without
generating a model response.
It returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves when the content has been
successfully loaded into context.
Use this method to preload a context before asking the model a question.
.PP
A context may be a document, conversation, history, or background
information.
You can call the \f[CR]append()\f[R] method at any point during the
session\(cqs lifetime.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
append(input)
append(input, options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]input\f[R]
The content to append to the context window.
This is either:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
A string \(em Shorthand for a single textual message.
.IP \(bu 2
An array of objects, each representing a single message in a
conversation with a language model.
Objects may have the following properties:
.RS 2
.TP
\f[B]role\f[R]
A string indicating the point of view the message is phrased from.
Must be one of:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]system\f[R]
A system\-level instruction that guides the model\(cqs overall behavior.
This must be the first instruction passed to the model.
.TP
\f[B]user\f[R]
A message from the user, which the API should respond to.
.TP
\f[B]assistant\f[R]
An input that provides context for the AI assistant, such as its persona
or the format of its responses.
Such messages mainly serve to provide context/history, and further shape
how the model responds.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]content\f[R]
A string representing a textual prompt, or an array of objects.
Each object includes the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
An enumerated value representing the type of content.
This can be one of:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]audio\f[R]
Audio content.
.TP
\f[B]image\f[R]
Image content.
.TP
\f[B]text\f[R]
Textual content.
.TP
\f[B]tool\-call\f[R]
A tool invocation issued by the model.
.TP
\f[B]tool\-response\f[R]
The result of a tool invocation.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]value\f[R]
The content of the message.
If the \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]text\f[R], this is always a string.
If the \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]audio\f[R] or \f[CR]image\f[R], the
\f[CR]value\f[R] can be one of several different object types; see What
data types are accepted?.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]prefix\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean, defaulting to \f[CR]false\f[R].
When \f[CR]true\f[R], the message is treated as a prefix for the
model\(cqs next generated response rather than a complete turn.
.RE
.RE
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An object representing the options that can be passed.
Properties include:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]signal\f[R]
An \f[CR]AbortSignal\f[R] to cancel the append operation.
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with \f[CR]undefined\f[R] when the
content has been prefilled into the context window, or rejects with one
of the following exception values on failure.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]AbortError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the operation was canceled via the \f[CR]signal\f[R] option.
.TP
\f[B]NotAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if usage of the method is blocked by a \f[CR]language\-model\f[R]
\f[CR]Permissions\-Policy\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]NotSupportedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]role\f[R] is \f[CR]assistant\f[R] and its
\f[CR]type\f[R] is anything other than \f[CR]text\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]text\f[R] and its
\f[CR]value\f[R] is not a string.
.IP \(bu 2
The input or output text is in a language the user agent doesn\(cqt
support for prompting.
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]image\f[R] or \f[CR]audio\f[R]
but the type was not listed in \f[CR]expectedInputs\f[R], or the
\f[CR]value\f[R] is not an accepted data type.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]OperationError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if prefilling fails for any other reason not listed in the other
exception types.
.TP
\f[B]QuotaExceededError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if appending \f[CR]input\f[R] would cause the session\(cqs
context usage to exceed the model\(cqs
\f[CR]LanguageModel.contextWindow\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]SyntaxError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
No messages are included in the messages array.
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]prefix\f[R] property is set to \f[CR]true\f[R] and:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
The message\(cqs \f[CR]role\f[R] is not \f[CR]assistant\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The message is not the last item in the messages array.
.RE
.RE
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if a message\(cqs \f[CR]role\f[R] is \f[CR]system\f[R] but it was
not the first message passed to the context.
.SH EXAMPLES
See also Adding context with initial and ongoing prompt inputs >
Appending extra messages to the context.
.SS Append context before prompting
This example shows how to append to a context for the user role before
calling \f[CR]prompt()\f[R].
Note that we can just specify text input (\f[CR]documentText\f[R]) in
this case, because \f[CR]user\f[R] is the default role.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] documentText = \(dqThis is my important essay...\(dq;
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();

\f[I]// Preload the document text into context\f[R]
\f[B]await\f[R] session.append(documentText);

\f[I]// Now ask questions about the document\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] summary = \f[B]await\f[R] session.prompt(
  \(dqSummarize the key points of this document.\(dq,
);
console.log(summary);
.EE
.SS Appending context with an abort signal
An abort signal lets you cancel an append operation.
The example below passes an \f[CR]AbortSignal\f[R] to the
\f[CR]signal\f[R] member and calls its \f[CR]abort()\f[R] method after 3
seconds.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] controller = \f[B]new\f[R] AbortController();
setTimeout(() \f[B]=>\f[R] controller.abort(), 3000);

\f[B]try\f[R] {
  \f[B]await\f[R] session.append(
    \(dqHere is some background context for future questions.\(dq,
    {
      signal: controller.signal,
    },
  );
  console.log(\(dqContext appended successfully.\(dq);
} \f[B]catch\f[R] (err) {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (err.name === \(dqAbortError\(dq) {
    console.log(\(dqAppend was aborted.\(dq);
  }
}
.EE
.SS Checking context usage after appending
The code below shows how to log the number of tokens used after
appending a large amount of context.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] largeDocument = \(dqThis is my large body of text...\(dq;
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();
\f[B]await\f[R] session.append(largeDocument);

console.log(
  \(gaContext used: ${session.contextUsage} / ${session.contextWindow} tokens\(ga,
);
.EE
